sc.manual.safety.corrosive.1=Carry them only in PTFE pipes: any other pipe breaks after about 10 seconds of contact and the fluid is lost.
sc.manual.safety.corrosive.2=Machines themselves are not harmed. Don't mix different fluids in one pipe.
sc.manual.safety.corrosivehead=Corrosive and toxic fluids
sc.manual.safety.explosions.1=Overvoltage: energy above a machine's tier destroys it in a blast of power %s + the tier difference - it hurts and knocks back, but breaks no blocks around. A cable above its tier burns out without a blast (smoke and a hiss). New machines, generators and storages are placed switched off - nothing can overload them until you switch them on.
sc.manual.safety.explosions.2=Heat-building machines pause at full heat instead of exploding, but run slower - let them cool.
sc.manual.safety.explosions.3=Once ignited the Fusion Reactor puts out EV-tier power - connect it with cable of EV tier or higher (superconductor and up), or the cable burns out.
sc.manual.safety.explosionshead=Explosions
sc.manual.safety.radiationhead=Radiation
sc.manual.safety.suit.1=At 80% heat the suit slows you, at 100% it shuts the chips off and adds weakness. Fewer high-tier chips or a higher suit mean less heat.
sc.manual.safety.suithead=Suit overheating
