sc.manual.field.funchead=Functions (the "Functions" tab)
sc.manual.field.functions.1=Each function is switched on and off on its own; switched-on protections add to the upkeep. No spawning: the chosen targets don't spawn inside (those already in are pushed out). No ender teleport: endermen can't teleport in. Hurt mobs: switch off to only push. Targets: hostiles; neutrals too (wild wolves, bats, squid); or every creature but animals, villagers, golems and pets.
sc.manual.field.functions.2=Warnings: the owner is told when the buffer is under a tenth and when the field goes down. Wireless charging (the Functions tab, Charging page): the mod's items, IC2's (EU) and other mods' RF items of the owner and the access list inside charge from the field's buffer - up to 10240 EU/s per player, x2 per charge booster upgrade (up to 4). Pick the priority (armour / hand / evenly / armour only), a buffer reserve charging leaves alone, and sparks from a node to the player. Heal allies: half a heart a second for 400 EU.
sc.manual.field.accesshead=Owner and private zone (the "Access" tab)
sc.manual.field.access.1=The owner is who placed the generator. The owner and their access list (up to 16 names) change the settings, only the owner edits the list. Private zone: strangers can't break or place blocks or open chests and machines inside; they can be pushed out of the field too (no damage).
sc.manual.field.lookhead=Redstone, look and map
sc.manual.field.look.1=Redstone at the master (Field tab): ignored, the field runs only with a signal, or a signal stops it - a stopped field uses no energy. The look is on the Zone tab: the outline (with the shell, always, only with a wrench in hand, never), running dashes, the shell, its animation (pulse, waves, none) and brightness, beams from the master to the nodes, a low hum at the nodes, and three colours - the shell, the outline and beams, charging sparks and flashes (8 ready ones or any with the R, G, B sliders). Where the field turns a projectile or stops an explosion a puff of the flash colour appears. The Map tab shows the field from above at its centre's height, the nodes and you.
sc.chat.link.noaccess=Link module: you need access to both clusters (owner or access list)
