sc.manual.energy.chargeslots=Charge slots by tier: %s. Each slot charges its own item at the tier's full rate.
sc.manual.energy.storage2.1=Under the charge slots is the discharge slot: put a charged battery there (the mod's or IC2's) and the storage takes its energy.
sc.manual.energy.storage2.2=Storage upgrades (the four slots on the right): a transformer raises the output voltage a tier, an energy storage upgrade adds +25% capacity, overdrive one more packet a tick (up to 4). Broken, the storage keeps its upgrades in the item, and crafting it into the next tier carries them over.
sc.manual.energy.storage2.3=The front (output) face turns with a wrench - right-click the side you want. A comparator next to the storage gives 0-15 by the charge. Hoppers and pipes reach only the charge and discharge slots, never the upgrades.
sc.manual.energy.powerhead=Power switch and redstone
sc.manual.energy.power.1=Above the energy gauge of machines, generators, storages, quarries and the field generator are a power switch and a redstone button. A switched-off block neither takes nor gives energy and does nothing - no line can overload it.
sc.manual.energy.power.2=Placed switched off: machines, generators and reactors, energy storages and charge pads, the field generator, quarries, the shower, energy transmitters, receivers and the quantum translator, the Armour Service Station, the Singular Station and the bridge controller: put the upgrades in and switch it on. With a cable or source above the block's input nearby (and no universal transformer) the switch is red, the screen warns, and switching on takes a double click.
sc.manual.energy.power.3=Redstone: always / only with a signal / only without one. "Disabled" - switched off by the button; "Stopped by signal" - held by the redstone mode.
sc.manual.energy.batteryhead=Portable batteries
sc.manual.energy.batteryline=%s, %s EU, up to %d EU/t
sc.manual.energy.battery.1=A battery charges and empties in an energy storage or on a charge pad (the battery's tier at most the block's), wirelessly from the field generator, and with IC2 in its storages and machines too. The charge shows on the icon (five steps) and in the bar under it.
sc.manual.energy.battery.2=Sneak + right-click with a battery in hand picks its mode: off, charge armour, charge the held item or charge everything carried (other batteries left alone). A green lamp lights on the icon while a mode is on. The held item isn't topped up while you dig with it.
sc.manual.energy.battery.3=Each tier is crafted from two batteries of the tier below - their charge carries over.
sc.manual.energy.slothead=Battery slot
sc.manual.energy.slot.1=Machines, quarries, the Exo rig and the field generator have a battery slot under the energy gauge: the battery tops up the buffer at the block's input voltage. Any tier fits - the energy comes out of the item, nothing can be overloaded. The button under it picks the mode: "reserve" - only while the buffer is under half (the grid first), "always" - keeps the buffer full.
sc.manual.energy.slot.2=On generators the same slot works the other way: the output charges the battery, no faster than the generator's output. Modes: "surplus" - only what the grid doesn't take (while the buffer is over half), "always" - part of the output goes to the battery even under full load.
sc.manual.energy.slot.3=The arrows between the slot and the gauge light while energy moves; the strip beside it is the battery's charge; the mode button's tooltip gives the rate and how long it lasts. Shift-click puts a battery straight into the slot. Pipes and hoppers put charged ones into a machine and take empty ones out - and the other way round for a generator. A switched-off block leaves the battery alone.
sc.manual.energy.fluidshead=Fluids by bucket and cell
sc.manual.energy.buckets=Every fluid of the mod has a bucket (%d kinds, in creative and NEI; R/U on a bucket shows where the fluid is made and where it goes). A bucket can't be poured out on the ground.
sc.manual.energy.fluids.1=Right-click a machine, generator or tank with a full bucket or cell (the mod's, IC2's or another mod's) to pour the fluid in, with an empty one to take it. The chat says how much moved.
sc.manual.energy.fluids.2=The tank extension upgrade (machines and generators): +%s mB to every tank per upgrade, up to %s. The cross over a tank pours it out for energy - 1 EU per %s mB.
sc.manual.field.targets.1=Targets: "hostile" - monsters only; "hostile and neutral" - every creature except players (pets of the owner and of the access list are left alone). Pushing out strangers is the private zone's, on the Access tab.
sc.manual.field.charginghead=Wireless charging
sc.manual.field.charging.1=The priority is picked on the Functions tab's second page (the list above). "Charge below N%" - items are charged only while under the threshold. "Batteries: skip" leaves batteries and crystals alone. "Full rate for each" (with a charge booster) gives every item the full rate, not a share of it.
sc.manual.field.rainhead=Rain shield
sc.manual.field.raincost=The field's upkeep +%d%% in rain, +%d%% in a thunderstorm; a lightning bolt falling into the field costs %d EU.
sc.manual.field.rain.1=A switch on the Functions tab. While rain or snow falls over the field: inside it none is seen or heard (at the edge the rain shows in part), drops burst on the shell, no new snow settles, water doesn't freeze. Snow and ice that were there before or put by a player stay.
sc.manual.field.rain.2=A bolt falling into the field goes out with its fire and strikes no one. Short of energy, the shield goes first and the field holds. Rain still puts out fire and waters farmland.
sc.manual.field.switchhead=The field's power and battery
sc.manual.field.switch.1=The power switch above the energy gauge takes the field down, and it takes no energy. A new field generator defaults to "no signal": a redstone signal switches the field off.
sc.manual.field.switch.2=Under the gauge is a battery slot: it tops up the master's buffer ("reserve" and "always" modes). Only the owner or the access list can take the battery out.
