sc.manual.energy.wireless.1=An energy transmitter takes energy from its grid and sends it to the energy receiver it's linked with, which gives it to its own grid through its front face. To link: a link card - right-click the transmitter, then the receiver. They work within one dimension; the range and the rate are the lower tier's of the two.
sc.manual.energy.wireless.2=A new link replaces the old one; "Unlink" on the screen drops it at both ends. Blocks taken with a wrench keep their link. The Beam button shows the link as a line in the world. The transmitter has a battery slot.
sc.manual.energy.quantumhead=Quantum translator
sc.manual.energy.quantum.1=The quantum translator (XV) sends up to 32,768 EU/t into any dimension, at any distance, with no loss. The link is an entangled crystal: sneak + right-click breaks it into two halves of one pair; one goes into the slot on the screen, the other into another translator.
sc.manual.energy.quantum.2=One end gives, the other takes (the Role button). The giving end pays a 2,048 EU/t upkeep. While the pair is up both blocks keep their chunk loaded and the halves wear about 1% an hour; a spent crystal must be replaced. Taking a half out pauses the link, putting in a half of another crystal makes a new pair.
