sc.armorfn.rad_shield.desc=Stops radiation: Quantum 75%, Exo 100% (25 less in Economy mode). Uses energy and heats the suit only in radiation: 20 EU/s (Exo 25) and 0.4 heat a second for each level stopped
death.attack.sc.radiation=%1$s died of radiation sickness
sc.manual.safety.radiation.1=RTGs and running reactors give off radiation. It falls with distance to nothing at the edge of the reach, and every block in the way takes its share: a block of lead lets 2% through, lead glass 5%, water 60%, any other solid block 70%.
sc.manual.safety.radiation.2=Radiation adds up from every source around and from what's in the inventory. A reactor gives it off only while lit and working; an RTG all the time it holds capsules. Radiation can be switched off or weakened in the config (the radiation section).
sc.manual.safety.radsources=Sources (level at the block, reach):
sc.manual.safety.radline=level %s, up to %d bl.
sc.manual.safety.radline.rtg=level %s for each capsule, up to %d bl.
sc.manual.safety.radline.carried=In the inventory: an isotope capsule %s, a stack of monazite ore %s
sc.manual.safety.dosehead=Dose
sc.manual.safety.dose.1=What gets through the protection builds up a dose: +1% a second for each level (next to an RTG 10% in 10 seconds, at an exo reactor 100% in 10 seconds). Out of radiation it falls 0.1% a second (from 100% to nothing in about 17 minutes). Death keeps it, but no more than 25%.
sc.manual.safety.dose.2=At once, while unprotected in radiation: on the way in a warning in chat and nausea; from level 1 steady nausea, from 3 slowness, from 5 weakness and strong hunger, from 8 wither, strong slowness and a heart of harm a second. By the dose: 10% - nausea; 25% - weakness and hunger; 50% - strong slowness and fatigue (slow digging); 75% - strong wither; 100% - a heart of harm a second until the dose falls.
sc.manual.safety.dose.3=A dosimeter in the hotbar shows the radiation, the dose and the protection in the screen corner and crackles the faster the stronger it is; right-click writes the readings in chat. Without one only a warning shows while radiation gets through.
sc.manual.safety.radprothead=Protection
sc.manual.safety.radprot.1=Walls: blocks of lead stop nearly all of it, lead glass lets you see the reactor. A lead casing (an upgrade in an RTG or reactor) keeps the radiation in, but the output drops 10% and fusion and exo reactors run hotter.
sc.manual.safety.radprot.2=The lead suit is cheap, 22% protection a piece (set in the config), the full suit stops 88%. But it's heavy: -15% speed a piece, no running in the full suit, a lower jump, you sink in water; from 3 pieces you dig slower; hunger goes faster. Against blows it's weak.
sc.manual.safety.radprot.3=The radiation shield of Quantum armour stops 75%, of Exo armour 100%. It uses energy and heat only in radiation: at an exo reactor (level 10) Quantum takes 150 EU/s and 3 heat a second - the shield alone holds, but with flight the suit overheats in about a minute and a half; Exo takes 250 EU/s and 4 heat of its 8 cooling. Empty or overheated armour doesn't protect - a warning flashes on screen.
sc.manual.safety.radprot.4=A field generator with Radiation shield on protects every player inside the field completely, for 300 EU a second for each level round each player.
sc.manual.safety.radcurehead=Treatment
sc.manual.safety.radcure.1=Radioprotector (a bottle, sugar, glowstone and carbon dust): eat it - dose -30%.
sc.manual.safety.radcure.2=Decontamination shower (MV): stand on it - the dose falls 2% a second, for 60 EU/t and 10 mB of water a tick while someone with a dose stands on the grate. Water by bucket or pipe.
