sc.manual.generator.bighead=Tokamak XV: the build
sc.manual.generator.big.1=The Tokamak XV (65,536 EU/t, XV) works only inside a 7x7x3 build. The middle layer: the Tokamak XV in the centre, 24 tokamak coils round it (every cell of the 5x5), round the edge a wall of lead blocks or lead glass. Cap and floor - 7x7 of lead or lead glass. The screen shows the build's scheme, what's missing in red, and in its bottom line what lighting still needs.
sc.manual.generator.big.2=Ports are the mod's blocks in the middle layer's wall: up to 4 tanks (liquid helium, hydrogen, argon, deuterium - the reactor takes what it needs, pipes come from outside) and 1-2 energy storages of IV or above - all the output goes there. A port shields worse than lead.
sc.manual.generator.big.3=It uses: liquid helium 3 mB/t (coil cooling, always in full), hydrogen 1 mB/t (heating; without it 70% power) and 50 mB to light (the charge is then 5 million EU instead of 10), deuterium 0.5 mB/t from a tank or cells 12 times faster, the Li blanket wears twice as fast. Deuterium and hydrogen go with the power: less while ramping up or with the storages full. Radiation 12 up to 20 blocks - the shell holds it.
sc.manual.generator.big.4=Stability (0-100%) falls without helium (-5/s), with the build broken (-10/s), from overdrive (-0.5/s a module) and plasma overheating (-2/s); otherwise it rises 1/s. At 40% and 20% - warnings in chat. Below 10% the reactor puts the plasma out itself with 1000 mB of argon from a tank. Without argon, at zero - a breakdown: a radiation burst of 25 up to 24 blocks for a minute, 3-5 coils thrown out, it needs lighting again. The Put out plasma button stops it safely at any time; after a stop or a breakdown it doesn't light itself again - press Allow lighting.
sc.manual.generator.big.5=The tokamak inside the build is walled in: its screen opens with an empty-hand right-click on any lead block, lead glass or coil of the build. The ignition charge is drawn from the port storages (charge them by cable from outside) - up to 131,072 EU/t. The plain tokamak (a ring of 8 coils) is a reactor of its own and doesn't go in this build.
sc.manual.ores.blockshead=Blocks of metal
sc.manual.ores.blocks.1=9 ingots of any of the mod's metals craft its block (as a block of iron), and the block goes back into 9 ingots. The blocks are a beacon's base. The refractory ones (titanium, tungsten, tantalum, niobium, hafnium) are harder and hardly mind blasts, the soft ones (tin, lithium, gallium, indium, magnesium) break quickly. The block of lead is separate - it's also the radiation shield. If another mod already has a block of that metal, 9 ingots craft its block; ours is then made from two of those, one on the other (two of ours come out).
