sc.manual.generator.big.6=The Tokamak XV's screen: on the left the plasma (the torus, a thermometer with the norm and the limit, stability, heat, power, a minute of stability), before lighting a readiness checklist; in the middle the build's scheme by layer (floor / middle / cap), the ports labelled with their tank's gas (E - a storage, ? - an empty tank); on the right the port tanks' gauges: sized by the tanks in the wall, a cross where a gas has none. A tank remembers its gas: an emptied one stays that gas's. The energy gauge on the right is the port storages' charge. Lighting needs at least 1000 mB of liquid helium and deuterium (a tank or cells).
