sc.book.ores.vanilla.link=Vanilla ores: iron, gold, gems
sc.book.ores.vanilla.intro.1=Ordinary Minecraft ores go into the mod's machines too. Iron and gold take the whole route "crusher -> washer -> centrifuge -> furnace" and give 2 ingots per ore instead of one; gold sometimes leaves a tiny pile of silver dust in the centrifuge. Crushed and purified ore can go straight into a furnace - also 2 ingots per ore.
sc.book.ores.vanilla.intro.2=The Crusher breaks coal, redstone, lapis, quartz, diamond and emerald ore straight into their drops - a little more than a pickaxe without Fortune, with a chance of a bonus. A quarry with the crushing, washing and centrifuge modules does all of this by itself.
sc.book.ores.vanilla.gems=Coal, redstone and gems
sc.book.ores.vanilla.extra=Quartz, diamonds and steel
sc.book.ores.vanilla.extra.1=Nether quartz is silicon oxide too: 2 quartz in the Crusher give 1 silica sand (quartzite ore gives 2). A diamond in the Crusher becomes diamond dust: diamond wire takes 1 dust instead of 2 diamonds, a diamond blade 2 dust instead of 4 diamonds. Iron dust with carbon dust in the Blast Furnace gives a steel ingot directly.
