sc.manual.singular.head=Singular Armour
sc.manual.singular.intro.1=The fourth and strongest suit (SV tier). It keeps everything the Exo suit can do - flight, the energy shield, annihilation, the fusion cell and the rest (Exo legacy) - on less gas. It follows the strict gas rules like Quantum and Exo: no helium in the loop - emergency mode.
sc.manual.singular.intro.2=It is made from Exo armour in the Singular Service Station (see "How to get it"); the station itself and the gravitational stabilisers are crafted on a crafting table.
sc.manual.singular.statshead=Stats
sc.manual.singular.stats=Protection: helmet %s, chestplate %s, leggings %s, boots %s - a charged set stops any ordinary damage. Each piece holds %s EU, charged at %s (%s EU/t): it needs an SV charger or a station with transformers.
sc.manual.singular.heat=Heat limit %s, passive cooling %s/s. Helium in the Singular chestplate's loop takes %s heat per 1 mB (%s in the other suits), each worn Singular radiator piece adds +%s%% cooling (+%s%% in the others).
sc.manual.singular.legacy=Exo legacy: every Exo function works in the Singular armour too, on %s%% less gas. A full Singular set also gives the Exo set bonuses.
sc.manual.singular.tankshead=Tanks (level 1)
sc.manual.singular.matter.1=A special fluid - Singular Matter (SM), a %s mB tank in the chestplate. The heavy functions, the upgrades and the conversion of the suit use it. Where to get it: the Matter Compressor in the "liquid matter" mode (%s mB instead of each capsule) and the by-product of a running Singular Reactor (%s mB/s). It is carried in a bucket or a Singular Matter Cell (%s mB) and fills through the Armour Service Station and the Singular Station (tank %s) and into the suit through the K menu.
sc.manual.singular.schemeshead=Colour schemes
sc.manual.singular.schemes.1=Each piece has its own colour scheme - the icon and the worn armour follow it. The default is scheme A, Violet Dark. The < > buttons of the Singular Station change it (free); the creative tab has the pieces in every scheme.
sc.manual.singular.next=Level modernisation (for the points and one task done), changing a branch and the colour scheme - in the Singular Service Station:
sc.manual.singular.fnhead=The Singular suit's functions
sc.manual.singular.fn.1=The suit's own functions open by levels: each piece has its own level from 1 to 5. Every worn Singular piece gets the level points: 1 per 10 mB of gases spent, 1 per 10 blocks of gravity flight, 1 per damage point absorbed, 5 per mob and 500 per boss (no more than 200 a minute from mobs), 2-20 per key function, 50 per new biome and 200 per new dimension. Thresholds: 2,000, 8,000, 25,000, 60,000 points; besides the points one of the level's three tasks is needed (shown in the piece's tooltip with Shift). Each level above the first: tanks +10 percent, protection from damage that bypasses armour +5 percent, EU use -5 percent; all 4 pieces at one level - another +10 percent. In creative mode everything is open. A locked function is grey in the K menu, marked "Opens at level N".
sc.manual.singular.fn.2=The drawback: below 10 percent of a piece's charge the gravitational flight, the event horizon and the anchor switch off. The Singular suit's own functions spend gas at their own rates, without the Exo legacy discount.
