sc.upgrade.tooltip.short.output_splitter=Storage: +1 output face each (up to 2)
sc.upgrade.tooltip.output_splitter=HV storages and up only: +1 output face each (up to 2, 3 outputs in all). Every output face is a stream of its own: the output voltage x (1 + overdrive) a tick. Upkeep: 1% of what each extra face gives comes out of the buffer. Every face that isn't an output takes energy in. Taking a module out resets the output set last
sc.upgrade.tooltip.output_splitter.noiu=Under IC2 without Industrial Upgrade a storage doesn't take it (IC2 takes one packet a tick from a block)
sc.upgrade.tooltip.howto.output_splitter=Put it in a storage's upgrade slots, then sneak + left-click a face with the mod's wrench - it becomes an extra output (again - an input again). The main output (the front) turns as before: right-click with the wrench
sc.upgrade.tooltip.short.adaptive_transformer=Storage: output up to the weakest consumer, at most its own +2
sc.upgrade.tooltip.adaptive_transformer=Storages only: raises the output tier, but no higher than the weakest consumer on the mod's network behind the cable on the output face or the machine right against it (and no higher than the cable's tier), at most the storage's tier +2 (up to SV). Behind an IC2 cable it doesn't raise: the consumers there can't be seen. No consumers or no known network - no raise. With several outputs the weakest counts. Plain Transformers work as before: the higher of the two tiers wins. One is enough
sc.upgrade.tooltip.howto.adaptive_transformer=Put it in a storage's upgrade slots and connect a mod cable with machines on it, or a machine right against the output - the tier sets itself, every tick. The current tier and what limits it are on the storage's screen
sc.upgrade.tooltip.slot.storage=Goes only into an energy storage's upgrade slots (not machines, generators or the charge pad)
