sc.manual.energy.storagemodshead=Storage-only modules
sc.manual.energy.storagemod.splitter=+1 output face each (HV and up, up to 2)
sc.manual.energy.storagemod.adaptive=Output up to the weakest consumer, at most its own +2
sc.manual.energy.storagemods.1=Output Splitter (HV storages and up): each module gives one more output face, up to three outputs. Set a face: sneak + left-click it with the mod's wrench (again - an input again). Every output face sends a stream of its own - the output voltage a tick, more with Overdrive; 1% of what each extra face gives comes out of the buffer. Under IC2 without Industrial Upgrade a storage doesn't take it.
sc.manual.energy.storagemods.2=Adaptive Transformer: raises the output tier by itself, but no higher than the weakest consumer on the mod's network behind the output cable (and no higher than the cable's tier) or the machine right against it, and no higher than the storage's tier +2. Behind an IC2 cable it doesn't raise - the consumers there can't be seen; no consumers - no raise. With plain Transformers the higher tier wins. The storage's screen shows the tier it raised the output to and what limits it.
