sc.cable.tooltip.singular=SV tier cable (131072 EU/t). No loss. Exo cables and anything below SV burn out next to an SV source - run SV through this cable only. Works in a bundle with a pipe and a pneumatic tube too.
sc.battery.tooltip.sv=SV tier battery: 16 billion EU, up to 131072 EU/t. Charged in an SV energy storage or charge pad, in a generator's battery slot and in IC2 chargers of tier 7; emptied into any storage.
sc.gui.xv.tier.sv=Output: SV
sc.gui.xv.tier.xv=Net output: XV (no SV receiver beside it); into port storages - at their tier
sc.waila.tok.nosv=No SV receiver beside it - output XV
sc.manual.generator.bigsvhead=SV output
sc.manual.generator.bigsv.1=When the Tokamak XV's energy goes straight into a net and everything beside it that takes energy stands SV (a SV cable with nothing weaker than SV behind it, a SV storage, an IC2 sink of tier 7 or higher), it sends its 65 536 EU/t as one SV packet. Otherwise it stays at XV (2 packets of 32 768), so lines on XV cables don't burn. Behind an IC2 cable SV is never used. It is checked every tick; the build's port storages always get no more than their input tier.
sc.manual.energy.cablesv.1=The Singular Cable (SV, 131 072 EU/t x 4 A) is the only cable that stands SV. IC2 cables (glass fibre too) don't.
sc.manual.energy.storagesv.1=The SV storage (about 2.1 billion EU) takes and gives SV. The Transformer upgrade raises the output no higher than XV - XV storages included, so XV nets never get SV by accident. Only the Adaptive Transformer can lift an output to SV (no higher than the storage's tier +2 and the weakest consumer past the output).
sc.manual.energy.transformersv.1=The XV-SV Transformer: the front face is SV (131 072 EU/t), the others XV (32 768 EU/t). Stepping up it gathers XV from the sides into SV packets; stepping down it feeds an XV net from a SV line. It is the main way to get SV from ordinary generators.
sc.manual.energy.svhead=SV tier - Singular
sc.manual.energy.svlead=SV is the mod's highest tier: %d EU/t a packet, four times XV (%d EU/t). In IC2 it is tier %d.
sc.manual.energy.svtext.1=SV is for moving huge flows of energy over long distances: one SV packet carries as much as four XV ones. There are no SV machines - SV energy is stored, sent and stepped down with transformers.
sc.manual.energy.svgethead=How to get SV
sc.manual.energy.svget.tokamak=%d EU/t as one SV packet when only SV takers are beside it
sc.manual.energy.svget.transformer=Step-up: XV in from the sides, SV out of the front
sc.manual.energy.svget.adaptive=In a QV / XV / SV storage: up to SV when everything past the output stands it
sc.manual.energy.svblockshead=SV blocks
sc.manual.energy.svblock.cable=Lossless, up to %d EU/t a net
sc.manual.energy.svblock.storage=%s EU, SV in and out
sc.manual.energy.svblock.pad=Charges armour and tools of any tier up to SV
sc.manual.energy.svblock.wireless=SV transmitter and receiver: range %s
sc.manual.energy.svblock.battery=Singular Core: %s EU, up to %d EU/t
sc.manual.energy.svcompathead=Careful: SV and IC2
sc.manual.energy.svcompat.1=In IC2 SV is tier 7: only sinks of tier 7 and higher stand it. IC2 cables (any) burn from SV, and IC2 machines below tier 7 blow up. Always put an XV-SV Transformer stepping down, then the mod's transformers, in front of IC2 machines.
sc.manual.energy.svcompat.2=The ordinary Transformer upgrade never lifts an output above XV - in generators and storages alike. SV is only ever reached on purpose: an XV-SV Transformer, the Adaptive Transformer, or a Tokamak XV beside a SV taker.
