sc.tooltip.matterCapsule=Fuel for the Singular Reactor
sc.tooltip.matterCapsule.details=Holds a singularity's mass: %s units of mass squeezed by the Matter Compressor down to the size of a nut. Feeding capsules raises the mass of the reactor's hole.
sc.tooltip.matterCapsule.howto=Made in the Matter Compressor (IV) from any items. Goes into the Singular Reactor's capsule slot.
sc.machine.tooltip.matter=§7Mass inside: §c%s§7 / %s
sc.manual.machine.matter_compressor=Matter Compressor: swallows any items and blocks from its inputs and keeps their mass in an internal counter, from which it presses Compressed Matter Capsules (or, in the "liquid matter" mode, pours Singular Matter). Heavy metals (lead, tungsten, hafnium, tantalum, iron, gold - ingots, dust, plates, crushed ore and their blocks) give more mass. It refuses: items with data (charged, configured, machines with things inside), upgrades, batteries and the capsules themselves; anything in a container (buckets and cells with fluid); machines, generators, storages, tanks and the mod's other blocks that hold something; rare items (a coloured name) and valuables - diamonds, emeralds and their blocks, ender pearls and eyes, nether stars, beacons, the dragon egg. The mass in the counter stays with the machine when it is broken.
sc.manual.matterCapsule=The Compressed Matter Capsule is the Singular Reactor's fuel. Inside are %s units of mass squeezed into a tiny dark core; the reactor feeds the capsules to its singularity, and each one raises its mass. One capsule lasts 5-10 minutes of work, depending on the feed mode.
sc.manual.matterCapsule.2=Capsules come from the Matter Compressor (IV), made of anything at all: stone is the cheapest (%s blocks a capsule), heavy metals the quickest (%s blocks of lead or tungsten). Keep a chest of cobblestone next to the compressor with a Puller upgrade inside - it takes whatever it finds.
