sc.manual.generator.sing.buildhead=Singular Reactor: the 7x7x5 build
sc.manual.generator.sing.build.1=The reactor sits in the centre of the third (middle) of five layers. Layers 1 and 5 are the floor and the cap, 7x7 of lead blocks or lead glass. Layers 2 and 4 are a 7x7 wall ring and a ring of 8 gravity coils round the axis, right under and over the reactor (a 3x3 without its centre). Layer 3 is the wall ring with the reactor in the centre.
sc.manual.generator.sing.build.2=Everything else inside is the vacuum chamber: it must be empty (air), the centre of the coil rings too. A block left in the chamber shows orange on the screen.
sc.manual.generator.sing.build.3=Ports are the mod's blocks in any wall cell of layers 2-4: up to %s tanks (liquid helium, deuterium, argon - pipes come in from outside) and up to %s energy storages, IV or better. A port held by another reactor or a Tokamak XV doesn't count. The screen opens with a right-click (empty hand) on the build's lead, glass or a coil.
sc.manual.generator.sing.fuelhead=Fuel and ports
sc.manual.generator.sing.fuel.1=Liquid helium %s mB/t - always, while it compresses, runs or is being stopped (lighting needs at least %s mB in the tanks). Deuterium: %s mB to light and %s mB/t while it runs. Argon: %s mB for one emergency soft stop.
sc.manual.generator.sing.fuel.2=Compressed matter capsules (the Matter Compressor) go into the slot on the screen: one is spent to light it, then the injector feeds them to the hole bit by bit. A capsule is %s%% of mass and lasts %s-%s minutes, by the feed mode.
sc.manual.generator.sing.cyclehead=The cycle
sc.manual.generator.sing.cycle.1=Preparing: the build closed, helium at least %s mB, deuterium at least %s mB, a capsule in the slot, at least %s million EU in the port storages (an SV storage, or several weaker ones). The "Light" button: the charge comes out of the storages at up to %s EU/t (~%s s), then %s s of compression - and a hole of %s%% mass is born.
sc.manual.generator.sing.cycle.2=Running: all the output goes into the port storages as SV packets (%s EU); the reactor gives energy only there. The "Stop" button eats the hole in %s s (the energy still comes, fading) and gives a fifth of the charge back to the storages - %s million EU. While the hole lives the reactor block can't be broken. Cancelling during the charge keeps what is in; during compression a fifth comes back.
sc.manual.generator.sing.masshead=Mass and its window
sc.manual.generator.sing.mass.1=The hole evaporates by itself (Hawking radiation), the lighter the faster; capsules raise its mass. The working window is 40-70%: exactly 131,072 EU/t there. A light hole gives more but radiates hard and may evaporate; a heavy one gives less.
