sc.manual.armor.gaseshead=Gases in the armour
sc.manual.armor.gases.1=Energy armour keeps its working gases in its own tanks - each gas lives in its own pieces. The suit's supply of a gas is the sum over the pieces worn. Below: what each gas does and how much of it each suit's pieces hold.
sc.manual.armor.gases.2=Without its gas a function works worse or does not switch on at all.
sc.manual.armor.gas.helium=Cooling the suit. The loop - liquid helium tank, pump and heat exchanger - is in the chestplate; without a chestplate there is no helium cooling, only weak passive cooling. Helmet, leggings and boots are radiators: each one worn adds 15% cooling and a little volume to the loop. Helium carries the heat away and slowly boils off.
sc.manual.armor.gas.oxygen=Breathing: the tank in the helmet, from Nano up. With Galacticraft this oxygen also lets you breathe in space.
sc.manual.armor.gas.hydrogen=Thruster boost: tanks in the chestplate and boots.
sc.manual.armor.gas.argon=Fire suppression: the chestplate's bottle puts out fire on the wearer.
sc.manual.armor.gas.krypton=The helmet's searchlight: a krypton lamp.
sc.manual.armor.gas.heavy_water=Radiation screen: a heavy water layer in the leggings.
sc.manual.armor.gas.deuterium=Fuel of the Exo's micro fusion cell in the chestplate.
sc.manual.armor.gas.singular_matter=Compressed matter for the Singular armour's heavy functions (Black Hole, Time Slow, Singularity mode), its upgrades and its conversion from Exo. Only the Singular chestplate has a tank of it. Where to get it: the Matter Compressor in the "liquid matter" mode and the Singular Reactor's by-product.
sc.manual.armor.gasfillhead=Refilling
sc.manual.armor.gasfill.1=The Armour Service Station and the Singular Station fill the gases: put the pieces in the slots or stand on the station wearing them. On the move the suit is refilled from the inventory through the armour menu (K), the Life support tab: with gas cells and buckets - one at a time or with the "Refuel all" button. Singular Matter goes in the same way from a Singular Matter Cell.
sc.manual.armor.station.1=The Armour Service Station (MV) fills energy armour with gases and charges it. Four slots - helmet, chestplate, leggings, boots; each takes only its own piece of the mod's armour.
sc.manual.armor.station.2=The station fills its inner tanks by itself from anything beside it that holds fluid: the mod's tanks and other mods' tanks, pipes and conduit bundles - on any side. A pipe may also push gas straight in. Up to 100 mB a tick of each gas. The armour is filled out of the station's tanks; the pumps spend 1 EU per 20 mB. The chestplate fills first (the helium loop), then the helmet, leggings and boots.
sc.manual.armor.station.3=Charging works like a charge pad: 128 EU a tick in all (MV), any of the mod's suits; with Transformers - at the input voltage. Stand on the station and it fills and charges the armour you wear, like a pad.
sc.manual.armor.station.4=The screen: the four armour slots on the left, each piece with a bar per gas it holds; in the middle the station's %s tanks with an x (pour out) over each and a check box under it - pull in and fill that gas or not; below, the filled / still to go line and the status. On the right the power switch, the redstone mode, the energy gauge and the Gases and He only switches.
