sc.armorStation.modules.tooltip=Upgrades: Overclocker (up to %d count) - gases and charging 1.43 times faster each, the pumps use more energy; Transformer - input one tier up, armour charges at the input voltage; Universal Transformer - any voltage; Energy Storage - buffer +%d EU. The upgrades stay in the item when it is dismantled.
sc.manual.armor.station.modules=Under the screen is a row of four upgrade slots, as on a machine. Overclocker (up to %d count): gases and charging 1.43 times faster each, the pumps use more energy, as machines do (x1.6 a tick, x1.12 per mB). Transformer: input one tier up each (MV, HV, EV and on), and the armour charges at the input voltage - with a transformer Quantum and Exo suits charge faster. Universal Transformer: any input voltage. Energy Storage: buffer +%d EU. No other upgrade fits. Dismantled with a wrench or broken, the station keeps its upgrades in the item and gets them back when placed; a placed station is switched off - switch it on once the line is checked.
