sc.manual.armor.station.tankshead=Inner tanks
sc.manual.armor.station.tanks=The station has %s inner tanks, one for each of the armour's gases, %d mB each. Each tank takes only its own gas. Pipes push gas straight into the tanks, and the station pulls it from the tanks beside it until its tank is full; the armour in the slots and on whoever stands on top is filled out of the tanks. A Tank Extension adds %d mB to every tank (counted up to %d); take it out and no gas is lost - the tank just takes nothing until it is used down to the new size. The x over a tank pours it out for energy: 1 EU per %d mB, only if the buffer pays for the whole tank. Pipes can't take gas out of the station. Taken apart with a wrench or broken, the station keeps its tanks in its item (shown with Shift) and gets them back when placed.
sc.manual.armor.station.windows=The two sides of the block have %s narrow windows, one per tank: each shows how full its tank is, in the gas's colour. Left to right: helium, oxygen, hydrogen, argon, krypton, heavy water, deuterium, singular matter.
