sc.manual.singstation.1=The Singular Service Station (SV) does everything the Armour Service Station does: four armour slots, %s inner tanks, charging, filling the worn suit of whoever stands on top, modules, pipes and buckets. It is placed switched off; the wrench takes it with its modules and gases.
sc.manual.singstation.2=Its main job is modernising Singular armour. A piece is ready when its level points are full and one of its next level's tasks is done (the tasks of whoever presses the button count). "Modernise" takes every ready piece in the slots up at once.
sc.manual.singstation.3=The screen: left the pieces with level and points, under them the slots of the open tab; centre the tabs "Upgrade · Convert · Transfer · Sync · Branches" - each with its own checklist (points, task, energy and each gas "have / need"), the multipliers, its button, the progress with the time left and the pause reason, "Cancel (50%)" and the status; a started process opens its tab by itself. The other tabs' slots are hidden and take nothing (what lies in them stays - the screen warns). Right the tanks and the energy as on the machines (x over a tank pours it out, a click on a gas label switches it), the modules, the colour scheme < > and a turning preview of the armour in the slots; at the bottom power, charge, fill, redstone, "Helium only" and "All gases". On a small screen (under 420 x 300) a compact window without the preview. Every condition has a tooltip.
sc.manual.singstation.costhead=Modernisation cost
sc.manual.singstation.cost=The table is the whole set's price (4 pieces); one piece pays a quarter. All four at once - %d%% cheaper. The time follows the dearest piece.
sc.manual.singstation.row=%d -> %d: %s EU, SM %d, He %d, D %d, Kr %d mB, %d min
sc.manual.singstation.process=The resources are drawn as it goes: energy from the buffer, gases from the station's tanks. Something short - it pauses, nothing is lost. The slots of the pieces in work are locked. "Cancel" (two clicks) gives half of what was drawn back; breaking the station or the wrench cancels first by the same rule. 4 -> 5 uses up the Singular Core in the catalyst slot at the start: its charge counts toward the EU, the charge above the cost goes into the station's buffer (what does not fit is lost). On cancel the core comes back with half of the charge counted toward the cost.
sc.manual.singstation.morehead=Branches, transfer, sync, scheme
sc.manual.singstation.more="Branches": switch the chestplate's branch at level 3 (press / grab) or 5 (black hole / dome) for %d mB of singular matter. "Level transfer": an old piece in the donor slot gives its level, points and branches to a new level-1 piece of the same type for %d%% of those levels' cost, and drops to level 1. "Sync": lagging pieces are raised to the highest one for resources, without tasks. The < > buttons change the colour scheme of every Singular piece in the slots for free.
sc.manual.singstation.stab=The Gravitational Stabiliser is a passive block: within %d blocks of the station horizontally and at its height (+-1) each gives +%d%% modernisation speed, up to %d count. A running Singular Reactor within %d blocks (resonance) adds +%d%% speed and -%d%% EU. While the station works, its rings spin faster, a hologram of the armour shows over the pedestal, the stabilisers' orbs glow and send beams to the rings.
sc.manual.singstation.tanks=Tanks: gases %d mB each, singular matter %d mB (a Tank Extension: +%d mB for it, the gases as the ordinary station's).
