sc.manual.singular.levelhead=K menu: level, profiles, cooldowns
sc.manual.singular.level.1=While any Singular piece is worn, the K menu has a "Level" tab: each piece's level and points (or "full"), the sync (all 4 pieces at one level - +10 percent more), the next level's three tasks with their progress (one is enough), "Ready for modernisation in the Singular Station" and roughly what modernising the set will cost and take. On the right: the branches of levels 3 and 5 (the first choice is free - here or on the chestplate's tab), the function profiles, the current level's bonuses and what opens at the next. On a narrow screen the tab splits into two pages.
sc.manual.singular.level.2=The "Combat", "Mining" and "Flight" function profiles remember which functions of every worn Singular piece are on; they are kept in the Singular chestplate. A profile's button switches the functions on and off as stored (an empty profile first takes the current ones), "Save current" overwrites the active one. The "Next profile" key (P by default when it's free; change it in Options > Controls) steps through them in turn. A profile never switches on a function locked by the piece's level or by a branch not chosen.
sc.manual.singular.level.3=Cooldowns on screen: above the hotbar, icons of the key functions (dash, press, grab, time slowing, black hole, dome, "Singularity") and Void rescue / Emergency heat vent while they cool down (the dark fill drains as the time runs out), "ready" for a few seconds after, a red "no SM" / "no gas" when a press would lack gas, the time left of the "Singularity" boost and weakness and of the time slowing, and a resonance icon. Where (bottom / top / right / left / off): the "Cooldowns" button on the "Level" tab. With the helmet's HUD on, the top left shows "Singular · lv N" and the active profile, the top right a line when a piece is ready to be modernised.
