sc.manual.comp.liquidhead="Liquid matter" mode
sc.manual.comp.liquid=The button at the bottom of the screen switches the compressor between capsules and liquid matter. In the "liquid matter" mode, instead of a capsule it pours %d mB of Singular Matter per %d units of mass into an inner tank of %d mB (a Tank Extension adds more). While the tank is full, compressing waits. The tank gauge with a "Clear" button shows on the right. By default the compressor makes capsules.
sc.manual.comp.cell=Pipes take the Singular Matter from any side, and so do an empty bucket or a Singular Matter Cell (right-click the compressor). The cell holds %d mB, pours into the Singular Station, tanks and machines, and into the suit from the K menu (the "Refuel all" button takes it too).
sc.manual.comp.mass=Mass: a block %s, an item %s, heavy metals %s times as much. Every %s units of mass make one capsule (about %s s at %s EU/t): that is %s blocks of stone or %s blocks of lead.
sc.manual.generator.sing.byproducthead=By-product: Singular Matter
sc.manual.generator.sing.byproduct=While the hole runs, the reactor gathers %d mB of Singular Matter a second in an inner tank of %d mB. Each second it flows on into the wall's port tanks that hold (or held) SM: pour a bucket of SM into one of the port tanks and it becomes the collector. Pipes, a bucket or a cell can also take it straight from the reactor block (when it can be reached). How much has gathered - in WAILA and in the tooltip of the mass line on the screen.
sc.manual.singstation.convhead=Conversion: Exo -> Singular
sc.manual.singstation.conv.1=The Singular armour is made of Exo. Put Exo pieces in the armour slots, the materials in the six "Materials" slots (one material may be spread over several slots) (the Singular Core may go in the catalyst slot as well), bring energy and gases and press "Convert". Several pieces are one process: the costs add up, the time follows the longest piece; stabilisers and resonance speed it up like a modernisation.
sc.manual.singstation.conv.2=The materials are taken whole at the start (the charge of an Exo Core and a Singular Core counts toward the EU), energy and gases as it goes; nothing there - it pauses. "Cancel" gives the materials back whole and half of the energy and gases drawn. The new piece is level 1, scheme A; the charge, gases (as much as fits), chips and switched-on functions come over from the Exo piece. A full set needs six kinds of materials (and a Singular Core) - six slots are enough to convert all four pieces in one process: 11 capsules, 8 Nb3Sn plates, a lens, a fusion core, an Exo Core, 2 hafnium ingots, with the Singular Core in the catalyst slot.
sc.manual.singstation.convrow=%s: %s EU, SM %d, He %d, D %d mB, %d min
sc.manual.singular.gethead=How to get it
sc.manual.singular.get.1=Each piece is made from the same Exo piece in the Singular Service Station: "Convert" with materials (compressed matter capsules, Nb3Sn plates and per piece a focus lens, a fusion core with a Singular Core, an Exo Core or hafnium ingots), energy, Singular Matter and gases. The Exo piece's charge, gases and chips are kept. Details and prices - in the station's article.
