sc.bridge.controller.tooltip=The brain of the Ground and Space Bridge
sc.bridge.controller.more=Goes under the middle of the bottom of a ring of gravity coils (5x5 - Ground Bridge, 7x7 - Space Bridge). Checks the build, keeps the shared gas tanks, bookmarks and the journal, opens the portal. Placed switched off.
sc.bridge.controller.howto=Right-click - the bridge screen: «Check», «Calibrate», target X / Y / Z, «Open». The wrench takes it with its gases and bookmarks.
sc.bridge.capacitor.tooltip=Stores energy for the instant birth of the singularity
sc.bridge.capacitor.more=Holds %s EU. Charged from the bridge's energy port, gives it all at once when the portal opens. Must touch the controller, another bridge part or the bottom of the ring (a chain of contacts).
sc.bridge.capacitor.howto=Place next to the controller or another capacitor. The wrench takes it with its charge.
sc.bridge.energyPort.tooltip=The bridge's energy input: EV...SV
sc.bridge.energyPort.more=Takes energy from any line up to SV, charges the capacitors and pays the hold of an open portal. Switched by the controller's «Power» button; switched off it takes nothing.
sc.bridge.energyPort.howto=Connect it to the controller by a chain of contacts and bring a cable.
sc.bridge.gasPort.tooltip=Gases and singular matter - into the bridge's shared tanks
sc.bridge.gasPort.more=Helium, argon, krypton, deuterium, heavy water and singular matter - by pipes, buckets and cells into the controller's shared tanks. Each extra gas port: +%s%% tank size.
sc.bridge.gasPort.howto=Right-click with a bucket or cell - pour in; an empty one - take out. Connect it to the controller by a chain of contacts.
sc.bridge.focuser.tooltip=Space Bridge only: focuses the puncture between dimensions
sc.bridge.focuser.more=4 of them on the diagonals of the 7x7 ring, one block beyond its corners: beside the controller (4 blocks left and right) and 8 blocks higher.
sc.bridge.focuser.howto=The layout is in the book, article «Ground and Space Bridge».
sc.bridge.navComputer.tooltip=Bridge module: accuracy and memory
sc.bridge.navComputer.more=32 bookmarks instead of 8; the nearest free place is searched within 32 blocks instead of 16.
sc.bridge.navComputer.howto=Connect it to the controller by a chain of contacts (next to it, a capacitor or the bottom of the ring).
sc.bridge.massCompensator.tooltip=Bridge module: lets mobs, items and minecarts through
sc.bridge.massCompensator.more=Without it only players pass the portal.
sc.bridge.massCompensator.howto=Connect it to the controller by a chain of contacts.
sc.bridge.ringCooler.tooltip=Bridge module: the ring cools faster
sc.bridge.ringCooler.more=Cooling after a close %s s -> %s s; spends %s mB of helium a second while the ring cools.
sc.bridge.ringCooler.howto=Connect it to the controller by a chain of contacts.
sc.bridge.portalShield.tooltip=Bridge module: hostile mobs from the far side don't come through
sc.bridge.portalShield.more=Monsters entering the far end of the portal stay there.
sc.bridge.portalShield.howto=Connect it to the controller by a chain of contacts.
sc.bridge.receiverBeacon.tooltip=A Ground Bridge target: cheaper and more accurate
sc.bridge.receiverBeacon.more=If the bridge's target is within %s blocks of a beacon (same dimension) - opening costs %s%% less (energy, SM, krypton).
sc.bridge.receiverBeacon.howto=Place it where you often go.
sc.bridge.dimAnchor.tooltip=The Space Bridge's anchor in another dimension
sc.bridge.dimAnchor.more=While at least one anchor stands in the target dimension, the Space Bridge costs half the energy there, less singular matter and no krypton at all.
sc.bridge.dimAnchor.howto=Take it to the dimension you open the Space Bridge to and place it.
