sc.manual.bridge.title=Ground and Space Bridge
sc.manual.bridge.about.1=A bridge is a generator of a controlled singularity. Energy is stored beforehand in Singularity Capacitors; when it opens, it all goes at once into a ring of gravity coils while singular matter "punctures" space. A vortex portal stands inside the ring and at the target: whatever enters one end comes out of the other.
sc.manual.bridge.about.2=The Ground Bridge (5x5 ring) goes anywhere in this world, the Space Bridge (7x7) to another dimension. Creation is instant: with enough energy and gases the portal appears right at "Open"; if not, the bridge says what is missing and how much. The portal lives a limited time, then the ring cools down. Recipes for the parts and items are at the end of the Bridge chapter's articles (and in NEI). The Singularity Capacitor is built round a Quantum cell and the remotes round a battery: its charge goes into the result.
sc.manual.bridge.groundhead=Ground Bridge: 5x5 ring, 3x3 vortex
sc.manual.bridge.front=Front view
sc.manual.bridge.ground.1=16 gravity coils form an even square standing on its edge - along X or Z, empty inside. The controller goes right under the middle of the ring's bottom.
sc.manual.bridge.ground.2=Capacitors, the energy port, the gas port and modules must be linked to the controller by a chain of contacts: touching the controller, the bottom of the ring or each other. The minimum: controller, energy port, gas port and capacitors for the opening.
sc.manual.bridge.ground.3=There must be %s free blocks on both sides of the ring. Gravitational Stabilisers (up to %s) within %s blocks of the ring make the portal live %s%% longer each and keep it stable.
sc.manual.bridge.ground.4="Check" in the controller shows on the schematic what's missing and outlines the first wrong block in the world for 5 seconds.
sc.manual.bridge.spacehead=Space Bridge: 7x7 ring, 5x5 vortex
sc.manual.bridge.space.1=24 coils and 4 Singularity Focusers on the diagonals, one block beyond the ring's corners. The other rules are the same; the gas port needs heavy water - the interdimensional puncture is radioactive.
sc.manual.bridge.space.2=The controller's screen gets a dimension choice. An Interdimensional Anchor in the target dimension makes the jump half as expensive.
sc.manual.bridge.calibhead=Calibration
sc.manual.bridge.calib=After building and after any change of a ring block press "Calibrate": %s mB of krypton and %s M EU, instant. The bridge won't open without it.
