sc.manual.bridge.remotehead=Remotes and the coordinator
sc.manual.bridge.remote.1=The Bridge Remote controls a Ground Bridge from afar, the Space Remote a Space Bridge, into any dimension (its key is a Singular Matter cell in its slot). Binding: right-click the controller with the remote - owner and friends only. Every opening command costs %s M EU of the remote's charge; storages, the charge pad and portable batteries charge it.
sc.manual.bridge.remote.2=A bridge answers remotes and armour only while its area is loaded: the controller has a "Remote mode" button - the area stays loaded for %s EU/t. Without energy the mode switches itself off.
sc.manual.bridge.remote.3=The Coordinator keeps one point: right-click a block - record it (marked "safe" when a vortex fits), Shift + right-click - name it. The controller takes the point from a coordinator in the inventory and writes its target into one, a right-click on "To C" copies a coordinator into an empty one (or on a crafting table: a filled + an empty coordinator - the filled one stays in the grid); a remote keeps a coordinator in its slot.
sc.manual.bridge.modeshead=Modes
sc.manual.bridge.modes.1="From base" - from the controller's screen: in at the ring, out at the coordinates. From a remote and the armour: "Home" - in next to you, out at the ring; "From me to a point" - in next to you, out at the coordinates; "From base remotely"; "Fetch a friend" - in next to the friend, out at the ring or at you; "To me" - in at the ring, out next to you.
sc.manual.bridge.modes.2=An end next to a player is a "projection": it stands %s blocks in front of the player, in the nearest free place, and the distance from the bridge to it is added to the price. No cooldowns - only the ring's cooling.
sc.manual.bridge.accesshead=Access and consent
sc.manual.bridge.access.1=The owner (who placed the controller) and their friends (up to %s names, kept by the owner) use the bridge and bind remotes and helmets. "Public" opens the controller's screen to everyone, but remotes and armour still work for the owner and friends only.
sc.manual.bridge.access.2="Fetch a friend" and any end next to someone else (within %s blocks) open only with that player's consent: they get a message with [Accept] / [Decline], valid %s seconds.
sc.manual.bridge.armourhead=The Singular armour link
sc.manual.bridge.armour.1=The Armour Link Module goes into a Singular helmet at the Singular Station (tab "Link", the module in your inventory). Then at each bridge's controller - "Bind helmet": up to %s bridges. The "Bridge link" function opens at helmet level 3.
sc.manual.bridge.armour.2=The "Bridge" tab of the K menu: the bridge, the modes, bookmarks, own coordinates with "Mine" and "Look" (up to %s blocks), history and the scanner's finds (the gravity scanner: chests, spawners, mod ores). A place check takes %s mB of krypton from the helmet. The armour is the beacon on your end: it is %s%% cheaper and precise; at level 5 - precise portals to the scanner's finds.
sc.manual.bridge.armour.3=Keys (set in "Controls"): H - "Home", J - open to the last target, Shift+J - remember the spot (where you stand - into the chosen bridge's bookmarks). While your portal is open, the bridge's line is at the top of the screen: time and stability.
