sc.book.bridge.stabcraft=The gravitational stabilisers by the ring are the Singular Station's ones: their recipe is in its article.
sc.book.bridge.modrule=The navigation computer, mass compensator, cooler and shield go like the ports: touching the controller, the ring's bottom edge or each other in a chain. The receiver beacon goes by the target, the anchor in the target dimension.
sc.book.bmod.navComputer=%s bookmarks instead of %s, a free spot is looked for within %s instead of %s, an unfamiliar target scatters up to %s blocks instead of %s.
sc.book.bmod.massCompensator=Lets mobs, items and minecarts through the portal; the price of mass and its hit on stability are halved.
sc.book.bmod.ringCooler=The ring cools %s times faster (%s s instead of %s) while there is helium: %s mB a second.
sc.book.bmod.portalShield=Hostile mobs from the other side do not get through the portal.
sc.book.bmod.receiverBeacon=Placed by the target: an opening within %s blocks of it is %s%% cheaper and precise.
sc.book.bmod.dimAnchor=Placed in the target dimension: without it the Space Bridge there costs %s times as much, and the first jump is a scouting one that scatters up to %s blocks.
sc.book.sing.fuel=Singular Reactor: fuel and cycle
sc.book.sing.safety=Singular Reactor: accidents and protection
sc.book.sing.buildimg=Layers from the bottom up: 1 - the floor, 2 - the lower coils, 3 - the reactor, the wall and the ports, 4 - the upper coils, 5 - the cap.
sc.book.singfn.title=Singular armour: functions and levels
sc.book.quarry.menuhead=The quarry's menu
sc.book.quarry.modules=Quarry modules
sc.book.quarry.exo=Exo Drilling Rig
sc.book.qmod.max=Counts up to %s
sc.book.exo.1=The rig digs nothing: its laser brings ore up from the deep - vanilla ores and the mod's. A haul costs %s EU, the base rate is %s haul/s. Speed modules make it faster (x1.4, energy x1.6 each), fortune adds copies of the ore (+50%% energy a level), crushing and washing +25%% energy each, the economy module -25%% energy and -20%% speed.
sc.book.exo.2=Ore lenses (%2$s slots, up to %3$s with resonator modules) raise their ore's chance: one lens x%1$s, each more adds another x%4$s; with the stabiliser x7 and +6 a lens, but a haul costs more.
sc.book.exo.3=The filter on the Output tab leaves ores out altogether (the "only these" and "all but these" modes). The deep scan module adds other mods' ores. Connect the rig to an XV network.
sc.book.exo.4=Below is each ore's chance a haul with no lenses and with one or four lenses on it (and no other lenses).
sc.book.exo.tablehead=Ore chance a haul
sc.book.exo.t.ore=Ore
sc.book.exo.t.base=Chance
sc.book.exo.t.lens1=1 lens
sc.book.exo.t.lens4=4 lenses
sc.book.exo.lenshead=Ore lenses
sc.book.defects.title=Defects and the Quality module
sc.book.defects.1=Many machine recipes have a defect chance: scrap dust comes out instead of the product, and the ingredients are spent anyway. A recipe's chance shows in NEI and on the precise machines' screens; the table below gives the highest chance among each machine's recipes.
sc.book.defects.2=Machines with heat: an operation interrupted by overheating (the heat reached %s) finishes with a doubled defect chance. Heat sinks and pauses prevent that.
sc.book.defects.3=The Quality Control module: defect chance x0.5 each, energy a tick x1.25 each. Two modules make defects four times rarer, four - sixteen times.
sc.book.defects.4=Modules of one kind count up to %s. Furnaces and the Matter Compressor do not take the Quality module: there is nothing to improve.
sc.book.defects.5=Scrap is not wasted: the crusher turns it back into silica sand.
sc.book.defects.tablehead=Defects by machine
sc.book.defects.t.machine=Machine
sc.book.defects.t.chance=Defects
sc.book.defects.upto=up to %s%%
sc.book.defects.recyclehead=Recycling scrap
sc.book.keys.title=The mod's keys
sc.book.keys.intro=The mod's keys are changed in Options - Controls, the Silicon Age section. The defaults:
sc.book.keys.t.key=Key
sc.book.keys.t.what=What it does
sc.book.keys.free=* - only if the key is free (not taken by the game, another mod or a suit function), otherwise unbound. "-" - unbound by default.
sc.book.keys.fn.1=Suit, blade and drill functions and the power modes have no keys by default: set them in the armour menu (K) - any key, with Ctrl, Shift or Alt, or the middle and side mouse buttons. Pressing it switches the function on and off; the dash, the annihilation pulse and the blade's strikes it fires.
sc.book.keys.fn.2=These are kept in the player's config/SiliconAge_armorkeys.cfg, not in the game's controls.
sc.book.keys.mousehead=The mouse and Shift
sc.book.keys.mouse.1=Shift over the mod's item shows the details in its tooltip, Ctrl - the controls and charging. Shift + right-click on a machine or generator with a weapon, armour, a blade or a drill charges it from the block's buffer; Shift + right-click twice with an empty hand empties the tanks.
sc.book.keys.mouse.2=In the handbook: Backspace goes back, a click on an icon opens its article, a right-click its recipe in NEI; the search is at the top right (Ctrl+F).
sc.book.keys.neihead=NEI
sc.book.keys.nei.1=With NEI: R over an item shows how to make it, U what it goes into (the mod's fluid buckets too). A click on the progress arrow in a machine's screen shows all its recipes.
sc.book.compat.title=Compatibility
sc.book.compat.intro=Silicon Age works on its own; the mods below are optional and add more.
sc.book.compat.ic2.1=One energy network: the mod's EU are IC2's EU; cables, machines and generators of both mods connect directly. The mod's armour, blades, drills and batteries charge in IC2's chargers and batteries, and the charge pads and the field generator charge IC2's items too.
sc.book.compat.ic2.2=IC2's copper, crushed ores and rubber fit the mod's recipes (through the ore dictionary); the mod's rubber is registered as itemRubber.
sc.book.compat.ic2.3=SV is IC2 tier %s: any IC2 cable burns from it and IC2 machines below that tier explode. Step it down with an XV-SV transformer before IC2.
sc.book.compat.iu.1=Only with Industrial Upgrade do the overdrive and the output splitter work in a storage that feeds an IC2 network (IC2 itself takes one packet a tick from a block). Without IC2 the mod's own network honours them anyway.
sc.book.compat.nei.1=Recipe pages for every machine and generator - with fluids, by-product and defect chances and EU/t; the Matter Compressor and the armour conversion in the Singular Station. A click on the progress arrow in a machine's screen opens its recipes; a right-click on an icon in the handbook - the item's recipe.
sc.book.compat.waila.1=Look-at info on the mod's blocks: charge and output, machine progress, tank contents, wireless links, radiation.
sc.book.compat.gc.1=On Galacticraft's airless worlds a suit helmet with breathing on and oxygen in its tank replaces the oxygen gear: %s mB of oxygen a second.
sc.book.compat.othershead=Other mods
sc.book.compat.others.1=Wrenches of BuildCraft, Thermal Expansion, Ender IO and other mods turn machines, generators, transformers, the quarry and the wireless blocks and work on conduit bundles. The field generator charges RF items too (Thermal Expansion, Ender IO and others): %s RF for 1 EU.
sc.book.multiplayer.title=The owner and multiplayer
sc.book.mp.intro=The field generator, the quarry, the wireless blocks and the bridge remember who placed them. Another player may open their screen but not change the settings - the buttons are dimmed.
sc.book.mp.field.1=The field's settings are changed by the owner and their access list (up to %s names); the list itself only by the owner. A private zone keeps others from breaking and placing blocks and opening chests and machines inside the field.
sc.book.mp.field.2=A generator placed next to someone else's field is placed switched off; fields can be linked with the link module only with access to both.
sc.book.mp.quarry.1=Only the owner (and server operators) can set the quarry up. The quarry digs on the owner's behalf: it leaves others' private field zones alone and respects other mods' land protection.
sc.book.mp.wireless.1=Only the owner (anyone in creative mode) can link a transmitter and a receiver with the link card, change their settings and take items from their slots.
sc.book.mp.bridgehead=The bridge
sc.book.mp.bridge.1=The controller's owner and their friends (up to %s names) use the bridge and bind remotes and helmets; "Public" opens the controller's screen to everyone, but remotes and armour work for the owner and friends only. Only the owner changes the bridge's name, the friend list and the access mode.
sc.book.mp.bridge.2=An end next to another player (within %s blocks) and "Fetch a friend" open only with their consent: they get a request with [Accept] / [Decline] buttons, valid for %s seconds.
sc.book.mp.otherhead=Everything else
sc.book.mp.other.1=Machines, generators, storages, stations and conduits have no owner - protect them with a field generator's private zone. The quantum translator is linked by the halves of an entangled crystal: whoever holds the other half connects.
sc.book.fluidlist.title=The mod's fluids and gases
sc.book.fluidlist.intro=All %s fluids and gases of the mod: what each is, where it is made and where it is needed (the lists come from the machine recipes and the generators' fuels). Fluids live in tanks, pipes, cells and buckets - they cannot be poured into the world.
sc.book.fluid.corrosive=Corrosive: only chemically resistant pipes hold it.
sc.book.fluid.used=Needed by: %s
sc.book.fluid.armor=armour (suit gases)
sc.book.fluid.bridge=the bridge
sc.book.fluid.d.hcl=Hydrochloric acid: chlorinates metallurgical silicon into trichlorosilane.
sc.book.fluid.d.sihcl3=Trichlorosilane: the CVD chamber deposits electronic-grade silicon from it.
sc.book.fluid.d.hydrogen=Hydrogen: a reducing agent and a fuel.
sc.book.fluid.d.oxygen=Oxygen: an oxidiser; the armour breathes it too.
sc.book.fluid.d.nitrogen=Nitrogen: an inert gas from the air separator.
sc.book.fluid.d.argon=Argon: an inert gas - sputtering, plasma, stabilising reactors and the bridge.
sc.book.fluid.d.krypton=Krypton: a rare gas from the air separator.
sc.book.fluid.d.fluorine=Fluorine: the mod's most corrosive gas.
sc.book.fluid.d.photoresist=Photoresist: the light-sensitive coat of a wafer before exposure.
sc.book.fluid.d.developer=Developer: washes off the exposed resist.
sc.book.fluid.d.hf=Hydrofluoric acid: etches silicon oxide.
sc.book.fluid.d.ph3=Phosphine: an n-type dopant gas.
sc.book.fluid.d.bcl3=Boron trichloride: a p-type dopant gas.
sc.book.fluid.d.ash3=Arsine: an n-type dopant gas (arsenic).
sc.book.fluid.d.naoh=Caustic soda: the alkali of chlor-alkali electrolysis.
sc.book.fluid.d.chlorine=Chlorine: from chlor-alkali electrolysis.
sc.book.fluid.d.steam=Steam: from the boilers, it drives the steam turbine.
sc.book.fluid.d.crudeoil=Crude oil: the refinery's feedstock.
sc.book.fluid.d.diesel=Diesel: a liquid fuel.
sc.book.fluid.d.liquidhelium=Liquid helium: the coolant of superconductors, reactors, armour and the bridge.
sc.book.fluid.d.deuterium=Deuterium: heavy hydrogen, the fusion reactors' fuel.
sc.book.fluid.d.ticl4=Titanium tetrachloride: the Kroll process intermediate.
sc.book.fluid.d.heavywater=Heavy water (D2O): electrolysed into deuterium.
sc.book.fluid.d.singularmatter=Singular matter: compressed mass for the Singular armour, cells and the bridge.
sc.book.modules.title=All modules
sc.book.modules.intro=Every module and upgrade of the mod in one place: what each does and where it goes. Details follow the links.
