sc.book.modules.o.fieldlink=Links field generators: right-click one, then the other.
sc.book.modules.o.bridgelink=Fitted into the Singular helmet at the Singular Station: links the armour to bridges.
sc.book.modules.o.tubespeed=Goes into an Extract connector slot of a pneumatic tube: items are pulled faster.
sc.book.modules.o.filter=A pneumatic tube connector's filter: samples, a white or black list (the advanced one also NBT and the ore dictionary).
sc.book.modules.o.orelens=Into the Exo Drilling Rig: multiplies its ore's chance.
sc.book.modules.o.areacard=Right-click two blocks for the corners; in the quarry's card slot it digs that box.
sc.book.modules.o.orescanner=Into the quarry's scanner slot: the Map tab shows the ore found.
sc.book.modules.o.chip=Chips go into the chestplate (right-click with a chip while wearing it) and give the suit its properties.
sc.book.mat.title=Components and materials
sc.book.mat.intro=Parts, intermediate materials and machine consumables. Each shows what it is, where it is made and what it goes into: the lists come from the machine, crafting table and furnace recipes, so they always match the game.
sc.book.mat.hint=G over any of these items opens its group; R and U in NEI show every recipe.
sc.book.mat.made=Made in: %s
sc.book.mat.used=Goes into: %s
sc.book.mat.usedby=Processed in: %s
sc.book.mat.more=and %s more
sc.book.mat.tool=A consumable: each operation takes 1 point of durability, %s in all.
sc.book.mat.head=A quarry drill head: %s blocks/s (x the quarry tier's speed), lasts %s blocks. %s.
sc.book.mat.headexo=A quarry drill head: %s blocks/s, never wears out, but energy x1.5. %s.
sc.book.mat_electronics.title=Electronic components
sc.book.mat_electronics.intro=Passive components, packages, lead frames, optics and energy cells: circuits, machines, chips and modules are built from them.
sc.book.mat_structure.title=Structural parts
sc.book.mat_structure.intro=Frames, plates, casings and other parts of machines, generators, weapons and tools.
sc.book.mat_power.title=Superconductors, reactors and turbines
sc.book.mat_power.intro=The Nb3Sn superconductor and the parts of fusion reactors, the Exo tier and turbines.
sc.book.mat_ore.title=Intermediate materials
sc.book.mat_ore.intro=What ore turns into on its way to an ingot - crushed and washed ore, dust - the ingots themselves, and coke, limestone and rubber.
sc.book.mat_tools.title=Machine consumables
sc.book.mat_tools.intro=The silicon chain machines' tools and the rolling machine's press moulds: they are not used up at once but wear one point an operation. The quarry's drill heads and ore scanner are here too.
sc.book.mat_cells.title=Cells and replaceable parts
sc.book.mat_cells.intro=Gas cells for reactors and crafting, the generators' replaceable parts: the wind rotor and the RTG's radioisotope capsule.
sc.book.mat.kind.crushedOreSC=Crushed ore
sc.book.mat.kind.purifiedCrushedOreSC=Washed ore
sc.book.mat.kind.dustSC=Dust
sc.book.mat.kind.dustTinySC=Tiny dust
sc.book.mat.kind.ingotSC=Ingots
sc.book.mat.d.crushedOreSC=Ore out of the crusher: smelting crushed ore gives twice the metal.
sc.book.mat.d.purifiedCrushedOreSC=Crushed ore out of the ore washer: cleaner, with by-products.
sc.book.mat.d.dustSC=Dust of metals and substances: from the crusher, the centrifuge and chemistry; smelts into an ingot. Scrap - the machines' defects - is here too.
sc.book.mat.d.dustTinySC=Small by-products of processing; nine tiny dusts make one dust.
sc.book.mat.d.ingotSC=Ingots of the mod's metals and alloys: the main crafting material.
sc.book.mat.d.coke=Coke: purified coal, the blast furnace's reducing agent.
sc.book.mat.d.limestoneSC=Limestone: a stone found in veins in the world; the blast furnace's flux for metallurgical silicon.
sc.book.mat.d.rubber=Rubber: cable insulation and seals.
sc.book.mat.d.rubberBlue=Blue rubber: a kind of rubber for its own recipes.
sc.book.mat.d.rubberHeatResist=Heat-resistant rubber: for parts that get hot.
sc.book.mat.d.resistor=Resistor: limits the current in circuits.
sc.book.mat.d.capacitor=Capacitor: stores charge in circuits and modules.
sc.book.mat.d.tantalumCapacitor=Tantalum capacitor: a compact one with a tantalum oxide dielectric.
sc.book.mat.d.dielectric=Tantalum oxide Ta2O5: the capacitors' dielectric.
sc.book.mat.d.ceramicPackage=A chip's ceramic package: holds the die and takes the heat away.
sc.book.mat.d.leadFrame3=A 3-pin lead frame: the metal base of a package with its leads.
sc.book.mat.d.leadFrame16=A 16-pin lead frame: the base of a chip package.
sc.book.mat.d.leadFrame40=A 40-pin lead frame: the base of a large chip's package.
sc.book.mat.d.compound=Compound: the moulding mass that seals the die in its package.
sc.book.mat.d.hfo2Die=A die with a hafnium oxide (HfO2) dielectric: for tier III armour chips.
sc.book.mat.d.sensor=Sensor: a die with a focus lens - a detector for modules, instruments and chips.
sc.book.mat.d.lens=Lens: the optics of tier II armour chips and ore lenses.
sc.book.mat.d.quartzEmitter=Quartz emitter: a quartz chamber with a controller - the emitter of blades and weapons.
sc.book.mat.d.copperCoil=Copper coil: the winding of motors and generators.
sc.book.mat.d.energyCellLV=LV energy cell: a steel casing with wires - storage for batteries, modules and tools.
sc.book.mat.d.energyCellMV=MV energy cell: two LV cells with silver cable.
sc.book.mat.d.energyCellHV=HV energy cell: two MV cells with tungsten cable.
sc.book.mat.d.alFoil=Aluminium foil: the plates of capacitors.
sc.book.mat.d.alFrame=Aluminium frame: a light framework.
sc.book.mat.d.tiFrame=Titanium frame: a strong framework for high-tier machines.
sc.book.mat.d.tiPlate=Titanium plate: plating for machines, armour and modules.
sc.book.mat.d.wTiPlate=Tungsten-titanium plate: for the Quantum tier - the suit, the blade and the drill.
sc.book.mat.d.tiCasing=Titanium casing: the shell of hot and precise machines.
sc.book.mat.d.steelCasing=Steel casing: the shell of machines, energy cells and drill heads.
sc.book.mat.d.polymerPlate=Polymer plate: light plating for armour and weapons.
sc.book.mat.d.polymerHandle=Polymer handle: the grip of blades and tools.
sc.book.mat.d.ptfeSheet=PTFE (Teflon) sheet: resists aggressive chemistry - pipes and seals.
sc.book.mat.d.ceramicRod=Ceramic rod: the core of resistors; smelted from aluminium dust.
sc.book.mat.d.combustionChamber=Combustion chamber: the heart of the combustion generator.
sc.book.mat.d.quartzChamber=Quartz chamber: a clear quartz vessel for emitters, plasma and reactors.
sc.book.mat.d.wBarrel=Tungsten barrel: a weapon's barrel and the Quantum drill's spindle.
sc.book.mat.d.focusLens=Focus lens: glass and diamond - focuses the beam of weapons and blades, the base of a sensor.
sc.book.mat.d.sputterBacking=Sputter target backing: the steel plate that holds the target's metal.
sc.book.mat.d.nb3SnIngot=Nb3Sn ingot: the superconducting alloy of niobium and tin from the blast furnace.
sc.book.mat.d.nb3SnPlate=Nb3Sn plate: for the Exo armour, blades, drills and reactors.
sc.book.mat.d.nb3SnCoil=Nb3Sn coil: a superconducting magnet.
sc.book.mat.d.heLoopModule=He-loop module: liquid helium cooling for the Exo tier.
sc.book.mat.d.liBlanketModule=Li-blanket: the fusion reactor's lithium shell - it goes into its 2nd slot and is used up as it runs.
sc.book.mat.d.fusionCore=Fusion core: assembled on the EV upgrade station - it does not fit a crafting grid.
sc.book.mat.d.powerCoreFrame=Power core frame: the base of the Nano armour, the Nano blade and the Nano drill.
sc.book.mat.d.turbineBladeTitanium=Titanium turbine blade: pressed on the rolling machine with the turbine blade mould.
sc.book.mat.d.turbineBladeTungsten=Tungsten turbine blade: pressed on the rolling machine, it takes more heat.
sc.book.mat.d.toolDIAMOND_WIRE=Diamond wire: the wire saw cuts the boule into wafers with it.
sc.book.mat.d.toolDIAMOND_BLADE=Diamond blade: the dicing saw cuts a wafer into dies with it.
sc.book.mat.d.toolSEED_CRYSTAL=Seed crystal: the single crystal is pulled from it.
sc.book.mat.d.toolPHOTOMASK=Photomask: the circuit pattern for the stepper.
sc.book.mat.d.toolSPUTTER_TARGET_COPPER=Copper target: the wiring metal for the sputterer.
sc.book.mat.d.toolSPUTTER_TARGET_ALUMINIUM=Aluminium target: the wiring metal for the sputterer.
sc.book.mat.d.toolSPUTTER_TARGET_TUNGSTEN=Tungsten target: metal for the sputterer.
sc.book.mat.d.toolMOLD_PLATE=Press mould: the rolling machine makes plates with it.
sc.book.mat.d.toolMOLD_BLADE=Press mould: the rolling machine makes turbine blades with it.
sc.book.mat.d.toolMOLD_COIL=Press mould: the rolling machine makes coils with it.
sc.book.mat.d.toolMOLD_TARGET=Press mould: the rolling machine makes sputter targets with it.
sc.book.mat.d.toolMOLD_LEAD_FRAME_3=Press mould: the rolling machine makes 3-pin lead frames with it.
sc.book.mat.d.toolMOLD_LEAD_FRAME_16=Press mould: the rolling machine makes 16-pin lead frames with it.
sc.book.mat.d.toolMOLD_LEAD_FRAME_40=Press mould: the rolling machine makes 40-pin lead frames with it.
sc.book.mat.d.oreScanner=Ore scanner: into the quarry's scanner slot - the Map tab shows the ore found.
sc.book.mat.d.liquidHeCell=Liquid He cell: the coolant in crafting superconducting and cryogenic parts.
sc.book.mat.d.deuteriumCell=Deuterium cell: the fuel of the fusion reactor and the Tokamak - without it the reactor does not ignite.
sc.book.mat.d.isotopeCapsule=Radioisotope capsule: the RTG's fuel - it decays all the time it is inside; it is radioactive in the inventory.
sc.book.mat.d.windRotor=Wind rotor: goes into the wind turbine and wears while it spins.
sc.book.path.title=Progression
sc.book.path.intro.1=Routes through the mod from the first copper cable to the singularity. Steps tick themselves like the first steps: once the item is in your inventory.
sc.book.path.intro.2=Energy grows tier by tier from LV to SV; each tier opens new machines and generators. Alongside go the reactors - the late game's main power - and the energy suits. Read about radiation before the first reactor.
sc.book.path_energy=Energy tiers
sc.book.path_reactors=Reactors
sc.book.path_suits=Suits
sc.book.path_radiation=Radiation before the first reactor
sc.book.path_after=After the controller
sc.book.path.more=More
sc.book.path.tier=%s - up to %s EU/t
sc.book.path.gens=Generators: %s.
sc.book.path.machines=Machines: %s.
sc.book.path.d.lv=Copper, bare copper cable, the first generator and the LV machines - the crusher, the ore washer, the kiln, the rolling machine.
sc.book.path.d.mv=Steel and insulated cable: chemistry, CVD, the centrifuge, the MV upgrade station, turbines. The silicon chain starts here.
sc.book.path.d.hv=Titanium and tungsten cable: the blast furnace, the Czochralski puller, the stepper, the air separator, the refinery; the fuel cell and the plasma generator.
sc.book.path.d.ev=The superconductor: the EV precise machines, the EV upgrade station, the fusion reactor - the first reactor, read about radiation.
sc.book.path.d.iv=The plasma reactor and the nano solar panel; the Matter Compressor - a machine above EV.
sc.book.path.d.qv=The Tokamak - a reactor in a ring of coils - and the quantum solar panel.
sc.book.path.d.xv=The Exo singularity reactor and the Tokamak XV, the Exo Drilling Rig, the quantum translator; XV cables and storages.
sc.book.path.d.sv=The Singular Reactor and the Tokamak XV in SV mode; the SV cable, storage and transformer. Careful with IC2.
sc.book.path.reactors.intro=Reactors are the main power. Each next one is stronger but more demanding: ignition, gases, cooling, radiation. Protect the base in advance.
sc.book.path.rline=%s, %s EU/t; fuel: %s
sc.book.path.d.fusion_reactor=The first reactor: ignition by outside energy, a Li-blanket and deuterium cells. Its core is assembled on the EV upgrade station.
sc.book.path.d.tokamak=The same fusion reactor in a ring of tokamak coils - far stronger.
sc.book.path.d.exo_reactor=An XV reactor cooled by liquid helium.
sc.book.path.d.tokamak_xv=A 7x7x3 multiblock with lead shielding and gas tanks; it can put out SV.
sc.book.path.d.singular_reactor=The summit: a 7x7x5 multiblock fuelled by compressed matter capsules from the Matter Compressor; it makes singular matter on the way.
sc.book.path.suits.intro=The energy suits grow in steps: each piece is made from the previous suit's piece, the charge and chips carry over. From Quantum on the functions run on the gases in the suit's tanks.
sc.book.path.sline=Charges from %s, holds %s EU
sc.book.path.d.suit.nano=Crafted at the crafting table; armour chips go into the chestplate.
sc.book.path.d.suit.quantum=A Nano piece, two W-Ti plates and two ceramic packages on the HV upgrade station.
sc.book.path.d.suit.exo=A Quantum piece, two Nb3Sn plates and a He-loop module on the EV upgrade station. The armour service station fills the gases.
sc.book.path.d.suit.singular=An Exo piece turns into a Singular one in the Singular Station; then come levels and new functions.
sc.book.path.rad.1=The first radiation sources are the RTG and radioisotope capsules in the inventory, later the reactors. Radiation that gets through the protection builds up a dose, and the dose brings sickness.
sc.book.path.rad.2=Before the first reactor: make a dosimeter (the level and the dose), a lead suit and a stock of lead blocks and lead glass for the walls. The radiation shielding module in an RTG or a reactor keeps the radiation in, at a slightly lower output.
sc.book.path.rad.3=Got a dose - the radioprotector and the decontamination shower. Details are in the Safety chapter.
sc.book.path.after.intro=The controller is done - the silicon chain is behind you. Now the mod opens up: armour, mining, protection, energy at a distance.
sc.book.path.step.chip=The first armour chip
sc.book.path.step.station=An upgrade station
sc.book.path.step.armorstation=The armour service station
sc.book.path.step.quarry=A silicon quarry
sc.book.path.step.field=A field generator
sc.book.path.step.wireless=Wireless energy
sc.book.path.d.after.chip=A tier I chip is crafted at the crafting table; the upgrade station raises it to tiers II and III.
sc.book.path.d.after.station=The MV, HV and EV upgrade stations improve chips, suits, blades and drills.
sc.book.path.d.after.armorstation=Charges the armour and fills it with gases.
sc.book.path.d.after.quarry=Digs an area layer by layer; modules crush and wash the ore on the spot.
sc.book.path.d.after.field=A protective field: against arrows and explosions, a private zone, rain, item charging.
sc.book.path.d.after.wireless=A transmitter and a receiver carry energy without cables.
sc.book.path.after.more=Next come the reactors and the singularity: the Bridge and the Singular armour. Parts and materials are in the Components chapter.
