sc.manual.energy.convhead=Energy Converter
sc.manual.energy.conv.1=Exchanges EU for other mods' energy and back: RF (Industrial Upgrade, Thermal Expansion, Ender IO and others), Mekanism joules, Galacticraft gJ. Inside are two buffers - EU and the chosen energy - and a conversion between them: one way, or "Balance".
sc.manual.energy.conv.2=The EU buffer holds %s EU, the other one the same at the rate. The conversion loses %s%% (the Efficiency module lowers it).
sc.manual.energy.conv.3=The base tier is %s: a throughput of %s EU/t (or as much of the other energy at the rate) - for the conversion, for input and for output. Transformers raise the tier, Channel Amplifiers double the packets.
sc.manual.energy.conv.4=It is placed switched off: set the faces first, then switch it on in the menu. Broken or dismantled with a wrench, the block keeps both buffers, the settings and the modules in its item.
sc.manual.energy.conv.pairshead=Pairs and rates
sc.manual.energy.conv.t.energy=Energy
sc.manual.energy.conv.t.rate=Rate
sc.manual.energy.conv.t.buffer=Buffer
sc.manual.energy.conv.t.need=Needs
sc.manual.energy.conv.need.rf=a mod with the RF API
sc.manual.energy.conv.need.j=Mekanism and its card
sc.manual.energy.conv.need.gj=Galacticraft and its card
sc.manual.energy.convpair.1=The pair is chosen with the "EU-RF / EU-J / EU-gJ" buttons; only pairs whose energy is in the game are offered. Changing the pair turns what is left of the old energy back into EU, with the loss; with no room in the EU buffer the change is refused.
sc.manual.energy.convpair.2=Rates and loss are set in the config (section converter). The gJ rate is Galacticraft's own by default.
sc.manual.energy.convpair.3=Direction: "EU -> X" and "X -> EU" move energy one way, "Balance" keeps both buffers equally full, moving energy towards the emptier one.
sc.manual.energy.conv.faceshead=Faces
sc.manual.energy.convfaces.1=Every face (top, bottom, north, south, west, east) has its own mode - Input, Output or Off - and buffer: EU, the other energy or Auto. An Auto input takes both energies, an Auto output gives what the neighbour understands: RF to an RF conduit, EU to this mod's or IC2's cable.
sc.manual.energy.convfaces.2=For this mod's net and IC2, input faces are a consumer and EU output faces a source. A voltage above the tier blows the converter up like a machine (except with a Universal Transformer). The "Neighbour" column shows what is beside each face and which energy it understands.
sc.manual.energy.convfaces.3=The "All: In", "All: Out" and "All: Auto" buttons under the faces' table switch all six faces at once; "All: Auto" makes them outputs with the Auto buffer. The gauges on the right show the EU buffer (green, orange, red by its fill) and the other energy's buffer in its own colour - the fuller, the brighter; the arrow between them points the way the conversion goes. The detailed explanations are tooltips on hover.
sc.manual.energy.conv.modhead=Expansions
sc.manual.energy.convmod.transformer=+1 tier each (up to %s - %s): more throughput and a higher EU output voltage.
sc.manual.energy.convmod.universal=Takes any voltage without exploding; the throughput is %s's. EU go out at the Transformers' tier.
sc.manual.energy.convmod.storage=Both buffers x4 each (up to %s - %s EU). A module comes out only when the energy fits without it.
sc.manual.energy.conv.extrahead=More
sc.manual.energy.convextra.1=Output priority: which outputs get energy first when the throughput runs short - EU or the other energy. Input filter: for every face, which energies it takes.
sc.manual.energy.convextra.2=A comparator reads how full the EU buffer or the other one is (the "Comparator" button). The charge slot charges this mod's and IC2's items from the EU buffer, RF items from the RF buffer (or from EU at the rate).
sc.manual.energy.convextra.3=Without mods with another energy the converter has no recipe and isn't in NEI; one already placed works as an EU buffer.
sc.book.compat.convhead=Energy Converter: RF, Mekanism, Galacticraft
sc.book.compat.conv.1=Exchanges EU for RF (1 EU = %s RF), Mekanism joules (1 EU = %s J, needs the "Mekanism Card") and Galacticraft gJ (1 EU = %s gJ, needs the "Galacticraft Card"). Works with Thermal and Ender IO conduits, Mekanism universal cables and Galacticraft wires.
sc.book.compat.conv.2=The mod works without them as well: other mods' APIs are only looked up by name. Without the RF API, Mekanism and Galacticraft the converter has no recipe.
sc.book.compat.conv.now=In this game: RF - %s, Mekanism - %s, Galacticraft - %s
sc.book.compat.conv.yes=yes
sc.book.compat.conv.no=no
