sc.manual.gen.rules.4=A lit reactor (tokamak, Tokamak XV, exo) switched off with the power button or redstone is paused: no fuel, helium or Li-blanket wear, and it carries on once switched back on. The Singular Reactor can't pause - switched off, it keeps evaporating and using helium.
sc.manual.gen.rules.5=While a reactor is unlit and charging for ignition it takes energy at any voltage - overvoltage doesn't harm it.
sc.manual.generator.tokamak.note.1=A lit tokamak switched off with the power button or redstone is paused: no deuterium use or Li-blanket wear, and it carries on once switched back on.
sc.manual.generator.exo_reactor.note.1=A lit exo reactor switched off with the power button or redstone is paused: it uses no helium and stays lit, no new ignition needed.
sc.manual.generator.big.7=A lit Tokamak XV switched off with the power button or redstone is paused: no fuel, helium or Li-blanket wear, and it carries on once switched back on.
sc.manual.generator.sing.cycle.3=The power button and redstone don't stop a running hole: switched off, the reactor keeps evaporating and using helium. Only the "Stop" button stops it.
sc.manual.energy.tank.2=A tank with auto-output pushes its fluid into a pipe beside it by itself. Set that pipe's connector at the tank to Extract - otherwise the network pumps the fluid back into the tank, back and forth.
sc.manual.energy.piperules.4=Next to a tank with auto-output set the pipe connector to Extract: on Insert the fluid goes round and round between the tank and the pipe.
sc.manual.field.access.2=A private zone can't be switched on while the field covers blocks you aren't allowed to break (someone else's protection, say): you can't throw it over another player's base.
sc.manual.field.access.3=A private zone doesn't stop pistons, fluids flowing in from outside or spreading fire: Minecraft 1.7.10 has no piston event to catch.
sc.manual.machines.quarry.6=The quarry never digs its 6 neighbouring blocks: levers, the output chest, cables and pipes right next to it stay put.
sc.manual.machines.quarry.7=A block that costs more energy than the quarry's whole buffer holds is dug once the buffer is full, emptying it.
sc.manual.armor.station.5=The station serves only players with access: a stranger standing on it gets neither gases nor charge.
