sc.drillfn.grav_funnel=Gravitational funnel
sc.drillfn.grav_funnel.desc=Singular drill: a 7x7 face (lv 4: 9x9, Miner lv 5: 11x11) where you look; wins over 5x5 and 3x3. Argon from the armour's tanks - 1 mB per block beyond the first; without argon - the usual area
sc.drillfn.cross_link=Cross-dimensional link
sc.drillfn.cross_link.desc=The linked storage takes the drops from any dimension while its chunk is loaded (the drill doesn't load it). SM from the armour - 1 mB a stack; without SM or not loaded - the drops go as usual
sc.drillfn.drain=Drain
sc.drillfn.drain.desc=Water and lava in the dug zone and around it are removed, the zone stays dry. The armour has no tanks for water or lava - the liquid is just gone
sc.drillfn.replace=Block replacement
sc.drillfn.replace.desc=The block from the hotbar slot right of the drill goes where one was dug (while there are any). No chests or machines. The black hole doesn't replace
sc.drillfn.phase_dig=Phase dig
sc.drillfn.phase_dig.desc=Only on its key: the ore you look at is dug out through up to 8 blocks of rock (Prospector: 12), the rock untouched. SM 2 mB, 0.5 s cooldown. Switching it off here is a safety catch
sc.drillfn.black_hole=Black hole
sc.drillfn.black_hole.desc=A mode: everything in the zone is destroyed - ores and liquids too, no drops, no XP. Zone 5x5 (lv 1-2), 9x9 (lv 3-4), 12x12 (lv 5), depth 1 or a tunnel of 3 - Shift + wheel. Leaves bedrock, chests and machines, others' claims. EU x0.5 a block, SM 1 mB per 25 blocks, strong heat, 12x12: 1 s cooldown. Gives singularity crumbs. Sneaking - one ordinary block
