sc.nei.comp.clot.tip=9 singularity crumbs on a crafting table; crumbs come from the Singular drill's black hole mode
sc.manual.comp.clot=In the "liquid matter" mode a singularity clot isn't counted as mass: it gives %s mB of Singular Matter straight into the tank (while the tank has room). In the capsule mode the clot waits in the input slot.
sc.manual.singcrumb.head=Singularity crumbs and clot
sc.manual.singcrumb.1=Singularity crumbs come only from the Singular drill's black hole mode: one per %s natural blocks destroyed, an ore counts %s times. Blocks placed by players don't count (no farming), ordinary digging, the laser and the phase dig give none. Crumbs go into the inventory, or fall at your feet when it is full.
sc.manual.singcrumb.2=Drill points: sneak + right-click in the air with crumbs in hand and a Singular drill on the hotbar - the drill gets %s level points each (only as many as it needs to fill the bar are used).
sc.manual.singcrumb.3=In the Singular Station crumbs in the material slots pay for the singular matter of the drill's modernisation: %s mB each, at most %s%% of its SM. They are taken at the start and come back whole on "Cancel".
sc.manual.singclot=Nine crumbs on a crafting table make a singularity clot. The Matter Compressor in its "liquid matter" mode turns a clot into %s mB of Singular Matter at once; in the capsule mode the clot waits in the input slot.
sc.manual.singblade.intro.1=The fourth-tier blade (SV) for the Singular armour. It keeps everything the Nano, Quantum and Exo blades do (Exo legacy), and grows through levels 1 to 5 on top: forms, functions of its own and branches open as it grows.
sc.manual.singblade.intro.2=The Exo legacy functions cost %s%% less EU. It has no tanks of its own: the gases of the Singular functions come from the tanks of the worn armour.
sc.manual.singtool.gethead=How to get it
sc.manual.singtool.get.1=There is no crafting recipe. An Exo blade or Exo drill goes into the Singular Station's tool slot, the materials into the material slots; "Convert" makes a level-1 Singular tool of it. Charge, switched-on functions, settings and the link are kept, the colour scheme follows the station. Armour and the tool can be converted in one process.
sc.manual.singtool.levelhead=Levels
sc.manual.singblade.level.1=Level points (Soul harvest) come from fights with the blade in hand: 5 for a hostile mob (at most 200 a minute), 500 for a boss. With a full bar the modernisation is done in the Singular Station. The level, points and branch are shown in the armour screen (K), the "Blade" tab, the "Level" page.
sc.manual.singtool.t.level=Lv
sc.manual.singtool.t.points=Points to the next
sc.manual.singtool.t.opens=Opens
sc.manual.singtool.t.branch=branch choice
sc.manual.singtool.t.perk=the branch's second perk
sc.manual.singtool.modernise=Modernisation N -> N+1 in the Singular Station costs %s%% of the full armour set's row (the time as the armour's, 4 -> 5 with the Singular Core in the catalyst slot); with the armour - one process:
sc.manual.singblade.formshead=Forms and their attacks
sc.manual.singblade.forms.1=Shift + mouse wheel with the blade in hand - the next open form (or the buttons on the "Level" page of the K menu). The form changes the normal hit and the special attack - the "Form attack" function on its own key. A form the level or branch hasn't opened works as a sword.
sc.manual.singblade.formline=%s. Attack %s: %s
sc.manual.singtool.fnhead=Its own functions
sc.manual.singblade.fn.1=Switched and bound to keys in the "Blade" tab of the K menu; those the level hasn't opened are grey. Key functions go on cooldown after use (shown above the hotbar).
sc.manual.singtool.fnline=lv %s · %s
sc.manual.singtool.branchhead=Branches
sc.manual.singtool.branch.1=The branch is chosen once at level %s - free, on the "Level" page of the K menu; the same choice gives its second perk at level %s. Later it can be changed only in the Singular Station for %s mB of singular matter.
sc.manual.singblade.lastchance=Last chance (Guardian, lv 5): a deadly blow leaves you at 1 health instead - once in %s min, for %s mB of singular matter. Its cooldown is shown above the hotbar.
sc.manual.singtool.gashead=Gases and the full set
sc.manual.singtool.gas.1=The Singular tools have no tanks of their own: singular matter, argon, krypton and helium come from the tanks of the worn armour. Without Singular armour (or the gas) the Singular functions don't work, the Exo ones still do.
sc.manual.singtool.gas.2=With the full Singular set the tool counts as Exo for every Exo rule, is fed by the chestplate, and its functions' cooldowns are %s%% shorter.
sc.manual.singtool.keyshead=Controls and the screen
sc.manual.singblade.keys.1=Shift + wheel - the form; the keys of the functions and the form attack are set in the K menu. Above the health and food bars - the current form and its attack, above the hotbar - the key functions' cooldowns next to the armour's. The blade's colour scheme follows the worn Singular chestplate.
sc.manual.singdrill.intro.1=The fourth-tier drill (SV) for the Singular armour. It does everything the Nano, Quantum and Exo drills do (Exo legacy), grows through levels 1 to 5 and gets functions of its own, the black hole mode and branches.
sc.manual.singdrill.intro.2=The Exo legacy functions cost %s%% less EU. It has no tanks of its own: the gases come from the tanks of the worn armour.
sc.manual.singdrill.level.1=Level points: 1 per %s blocks dug (in any mode) and %s for every singularity crumb fed to it. With a full bar the modernisation is done in the Singular Station.
sc.manual.singdrill.crumbpay=Singularity crumbs in the material slots pay for the SM of the drill's modernisation: %s mB each, at most %s%% of its SM.
sc.manual.singdrill.holehead=The black hole mode
sc.manual.singdrill.hole.1=Shift + wheel with the drill in hand steps: normal -> %s -> %s -> %s (as far as the level opens), each size with depth 1 or a tunnel of %s. The zone is outlined in advance; sneaking digs one ordinary block.
sc.manual.singdrill.hole.2=Everything in the zone is destroyed - ores too, no drops, no XP; water and lava vanish, the zone stays dry. It never touches: bedrock and other unbreakable blocks, blocks with contents (chests, machines, anything with a tile entity), spawn protection, others' claims and fields, anything a break event refuses, unloaded chunks.
sc.manual.singdrill.hole.3=Cost: %s%% of the usual EU a block, 1 mB of singular matter per %s blocks, strong heat; the 12x12 zone has a %s s cooldown (none for the Miner from lv 3). Without SM the drill digs as usual.
sc.manual.singdrill.hole.4=Only this mode gives singularity crumbs: one per %s natural blocks destroyed, an ore counts %s. The count toward the next crumb is on the drill's panel at the top of the screen.
sc.manual.singdrill.keys.1=Shift + wheel - the black hole mode, sneak + right-click in the air - depth 1 / tunnel. Function keys are set in the K menu, the "Drill" tab. At the top of the screen - the drill's panel: mode, crumb, SM in the armour, heat; above the hotbar - the cooldowns (phase dig, the 12x12 black hole).
sc.manual.singstation.toolhead=The tool slot: blade and drill
sc.manual.singstation.tool.1=Next to the armour slots there is a tool slot (pipes and hoppers reach it too). An Exo blade or Exo drill in it is made Singular, level 1, by "Convert" (with the armour - one process); a Singular one is modernised and changes its branch like the chestplate.
sc.manual.singstation.tool.2=Modernisation: the blade pays %s%%, the drill %s%% of the full set's row. Singularity crumbs in the material slots pay for the drill's SM: %s mB each, at most %s%%. A branch change - %s mB of singular matter.
sc.book.path.suits.tools=The Singular blade and drill are got the same way: the Exo blade and Exo drill are converted in the Singular Station, then come levels, forms and the black hole.
sc.book.fluid.compliquid=%s (liquid matter mode, singularity clots)
sc.book.keys.mouse.3=Singular tools: Shift + mouse wheel - the blade's form or the drill's black hole mode (the hotbar doesn't scroll then); sneak + right-click in the air with the drill - depth 1 / tunnel, with singularity crumbs - feed them to the drill.
