sc.book.marks.empty=No bookmarks yet. The star in an article's header adds it here, a second click removes it.
sc.book.marks.missing=No such article any more (%s)
sc.book.intro.search=The search (Ctrl+F or /) looks through the titles and text of every article, tables and item names included; Enter opens the article right at the match. The star in an article's header bookmarks it, the ribbon next to it lists the bookmarks.
sc.book.keys.bookhead=The handbook: search and bookmarks
sc.book.keys.book.1=Ctrl+F or / - to the search line (or just start typing). From two letters the handbook lists the articles found: the title, the chapter and a piece of text with the match highlighted; first those with the query in the title, then those with more matches. Case doesn't matter, several words are found even apart.
sc.book.keys.book.2=Arrows up and down - choose, Enter or a click - open: the article scrolls to the first match and lights it up for a moment. Backspace goes back to the list, Esc clears the search, a second Esc closes the handbook.
sc.book.keys.book.3=The star in an article's header adds it to the bookmarks or removes it (up to 64). The ribbon in the header and the "Bookmarks:" line on the first page open the list: a click - the article, the cross - remove it. Bookmarks are kept on this computer, in config/siliconage-book.cfg.
